# What must never enter the build context.
#
# A .dockerignore is not an optimisation here, it is the control that
# keeps live provider keys out of the image. Without it `COPY . .` --
# or any future broad COPY -- bakes `.env` into a layer, and a layer
# is readable by anyone who can pull the image even if a later layer
# deletes the file.
#
# Deny-by-exception would be safer still, but Docker has no reliable
# "ignore everything then re-include" for build contexts across
# versions, so this is an explicit list and D1 verifies the result by
# listing the image filesystem rather than trusting this file.

# ---- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example

# ---- user data ---------------------------------------------------------
# Uploaded documents. These belong in a volume at runtime, never in an
# image: baking them in would ship one tenant's files to every deploy.
uploads/
uploads-e2e/

# ---- version control and history ---------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# ---- local runtimes ----------------------------------------------------
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---- the frontend ------------------------------------------------------
# The Next.js app deploys to Vercel and shares no runtime with the API.
# node_modules alone is hundreds of megabytes of build context.
web/

# ---- things that are not the application --------------------------------
#
# NOT excluded here: tests/ and eval/. The build context is shared by
# every stage, so excluding them would make it impossible to run the
# suite inside the image -- which is exactly how the runtime gets
# verified (R4). They are kept OUT OF THE RUNTIME STAGE instead, by
# copying only `app/` and `alembic/` into it. D1 proves that by
# listing the final image's filesystem.
scripts/
docs/
.claude/
.agents/
*.md
!README.md

# ---- editor / OS noise --------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
